---
description: Place new JS files in static/js subdirs (not root) due to .gitignore
globs: static/js/**/*.js
alwaysApply: false
---

# static/js File Placement

`.gitignore` has `static/js/*.js`, which ignores any `.js` file directly in `static/js/`.

**When adding new JS modules**, place them in a subdirectory (e.g. `static/js/views/`, `static/js/lib/`) so they are tracked by git. Do not add new files directly to `static/js/`.

Existing files like `app.js` in the root are tracked because they were committed before the rule; new files there would be ignored.
